# Line endings are load-bearing in this repository.
#
# Plan, config, source, and test files are hashed into provenance manifests — see
# plans/m8_step1b_ahmed_transfer.md section 4.3 (source_manifest.json) and section 5.1
# (approved_plan_sha256) — and CLAUDE.md section 3 rule 1 requires every recorded number
# to be regenerable. With core.autocrlf=true and no attributes, Git stores LF but checks
# out CRLF on Windows, so the same committed file hashes differently in a fresh clone
# than in a working tree that was never re-checked-out. Verified 2026-07-30: without this
# file, plans/m8_step1b_ahmed_transfer.md hashed fa64b234... in a fresh worktree instead
# of the recorded and reviewed 9294cb05....
#
# eol=lf makes the working tree byte-identical to the index on every platform, so a
# recorded SHA-256 is verifiable anywhere. Do not remove without re-deriving every
# recorded hash in HISTORY.md, HANDOFF.md, the plans, and any frozen manifest.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary payloads: never touched by EOL conversion. text=auto already auto-detects most
# of these, but scientific artifacts are declared explicitly so detection is not relied on.
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.bin  binary
*.npy  binary
*.npz  binary
*.h5   binary
*.mat  binary
*.xlsx binary
